### Description

The TypeSafe provider docs say the response carries the resolved version:

> Use `jev-latest` or another TypeSafe model ID. The response includes the actual model ID, such as the resolved version behind the alias.

Routing the same model through AI Gateway loses that. `response.modelId` comes back as the alias I sent, and no field anywhere in the result names a version.

I walked every leaf of the result object, including `providerMetadata.gateway.routing` and the raw HTTP body. 69 leaves, none of them a version. I also called `POST /v4/ai/evaluation-model` directly to rule out the SDK dropping a field, and the server response is identical, so this looks server-side rather than a client parsing issue.

There's also no versioned id to ask for. The catalogue lists 376 models with one TypeSafe entry, and every versioned form 404s:

