typesafe-ai/jev-1.13    Model 'typesafe-ai/jev-1.13' not found
typesafe-ai/jev@1.13    Model 'typesafe-ai/jev@1.13' not found
typesafe-ai/jev-latest  Model 'typesafe-ai/jev-latest' not found
```

**Expected:** `response.modelId` names the version that answered, matching the direct provider, or a versioned id is accepted on the way in.

**Actual:** both directions give the alias only.

**Why it matters:** I'm running an eval that has to attribute results to one model version. If a new Jev ships mid-run, the data mixes versions and nothing in the payload records it. The same run against the direct TypeSafe provider can record the version, so the gateway path is the one that loses reproducibility.

